  "body": "Positioned along Ralph Eagles Place opposite local school grounds, this 1,328sqm section is a raw, quiet slice of coastal land surrounded by mature greenery. Held under the Public Works Act and offered to the market as an untouched freehold parcel, it represents a direct opportunity to secure a significant footprint in an established coastal enclave.\r\n\r\nWhat You'll Love:\r\n\r\n- 1,328sqm (more or less) of raw freehold land held under Section 5 SO 473715\r\n- Completely untouched natural site with established mature trees\r\n- Generous total land area providing a substantial green backdrop\r\n- Straightforward crown process under official instruction\r\n- Positioned in an established and quiet coastal suburb\r\n\r\nLifestyle & Location:\r\nRalph Eagles Place sits in a leafy, settled pocket of Long Bay where quiet residential streets meet coastal convenience. You are just down the road from the paths at Long Bay Regional Park, the beach, and the local village square. It is a neighbourhood defined by its relaxed atmosphere, established trees, and strong local community.\r\n\r\nLand parcels of this scale are rare in Long Bay. Get in touch with Matt Corin today to secure this land holding.",
